-- fehendhoo
update nodes set attributes = coalesce(attributes, '{}'::jsonb) || '{"island_content_source":"legacy_mtg_guide","island_quick_facts":[],"island_overview":[],"island_sections":[],"island_faqs":[{"question":"How do I get to Fehendhoo Island?","answer":"Public ferry service operates weekly from Male (approximately 10 hours journey time). Private speedboat transfers can be arranged through guesthouses (approximately 4 hours from Male)."},{"question":"What is the best time to visit Fehendhoo Island?","answer":"The best time to visit Fehendhoo Island is during the northeast monsoon season (December to April), which brings dry, sunny weather with lower humidity and calmer seas. For manta ray encounters in nearby Hanifaru Bay, visit during the southwest monsoon (May to November). Water temperature remains warm (27-30C/80-86F) throughout the year."},{"question":"What makes Fehendhoo different from other local islands in the Maldives?","answer":"Fehendhoo stands out for its exceptional preservation of traditional Maldivian life within the UNESCO Biosphere Reserve. Unlike more developed islands, Fehendhoo maintains its authentic character with a community still primarily engaged in traditional fishing and crafts. The island offers access to Baa Atoll''s spectacular marine life while providing a genuine cultural experience away from mass tourism."},{"question":"Are there any dress code requirements on Fehendhoo Island?","answer":"As Fehendhoo is a local inhabited island with a Muslim population, visitors are expected to dress modestly in public areas (shoulders and knees covered). Swimwear is only permitted at the designated \"bikini beach.\" When visiting the mosque or religious sites, women should cover their heads. These requirements don''t apply during water activities or at resort day visits."},{"question":"What marine life can I expect to see while snorkeling around Fehendhoo?","answer":"Fehendhoo''s waters offer excellent marine biodiversity, including healthy coral formations with both hard and soft corals. Common sightings include reef sharks (particularly blacktip and whitetip), sea turtles, various ray species, and abundant reef fish. Seasonal visitors include manta rays (May-November). The house reef provides easy access to this underwater world directly from shore."}],"island_nearby_slugs":[]}'::jsonb
where node_type = 'location' and slug = 'fehendhoo';


-- felidhoo
update nodes set attributes = coalesce(attributes, '{}'::jsonb) || '{"island_content_source":"legacy_mtg_guide","island_quick_facts":[{"label":"Location","value":"Vaavu Atoll, Central Maldives"},{"label":"Island Type","value":"Inhabited Local Island"},{"label":"Population","value":"Approximately 2,100 residents"},{"label":"Size","value":"1.8 km long, 1.1 km wide"},{"label":"Distance from Male","value":"66 km"},{"label":"Transfer Options","value":"Speedboat or seaplane"},{"label":"Known For","value":"Magnificent culture, stunning beaches, excellent diving"},{"label":"Best For","value":"Culture enthusiasts, beach lovers, divers, adventure seekers"}],"island_overview":["Felidhoo Island is a magnificent local island in Vaavu Atoll that offers visitors a vibrant glimpse into traditional Maldivian life. This exceptional island combines natural beauty with an energetic atmosphere, providing an ideal destination for travelers seeking outstanding cultural experiences and stunning tropical surroundings.","Known for its beautiful beaches, magnificent coral reefs, and excellent marine biodiversity, Felidhoo provides wonderful opportunities for snorkeling, swimming, and underwater exploration. The island''s vibrant community embraces visitors with traditional Maldivian warmth and shares their dynamic way of life with magnificent hospitality.","What makes Felidhoo special is its magnificent natural environment and vibrant island setting. Visitors can enjoy stunning beaches, explore rich marine ecosystems, and experience dynamic island culture while staying in comfortable accommodations that showcase the magnificent Maldivian lifestyle."],"island_sections":[{"heading":"Location & Map","paragraphs":["Felidhoo Island is beautifully located in the heart of Vaavu Atoll, approximately 66 kilometers from Male. This location provides a magnificent and vibrant experience while maintaining excellent accessibility to the capital and international airport through various transfer options.","The island''s position offers excellent protection from strong currents while providing access to stunning coral reefs and diverse marine ecosystems. Its location in the atoll makes it an ideal base for exploring the natural beauty and cultural richness of Vaavu Atoll in its most magnificent form."]},{"heading":"Felidhoo: Magnificent Paradise & Marine Vibrancy","paragraphs":["Felidhoo Island is blessed with exceptional natural beauty, featuring stunning white sand beaches, crystal-clear turquoise waters, and one of the most magnificent marine environments in Vaavu Atoll. The island offers perfect conditions for beach relaxation and marine exploration in a vibrant, dynamic setting."]},{"heading":"Stunning White Sand Beaches","paragraphs":["Felidhoo features magnificent white sand beaches with gentle slopes and calm waters, perfect for swimming, sunbathing, and dynamic beach activities."]},{"heading":"Magnificent House Reef Snorkeling","paragraphs":["The island''s house reef is easily accessible from the beach and offers vibrant snorkeling with diverse marine life and colorful coral formations."]},{"heading":"Vibrant Island Community","paragraphs":["Experience the dynamic spirit of traditional island life with friendly locals and magnificent Maldivian culture in a vibrant community setting."]},{"heading":"Dynamic Sandbank Adventures","paragraphs":["Explore nearby uninhabited sandbanks and magnificent islands around Felidhoo for stunning tropical paradise experiences with rich marine life."]},{"heading":"Beach Features","paragraphs":["Felidhoo''s coastal highlights include:"]},{"heading":"Marine Environment","paragraphs":["The waters around Felidhoo feature:"]},{"heading":"Activities & Experiences","paragraphs":["Felidhoo offers a perfect blend of marine adventures, cultural experiences, and magnificent activities. The island''s vibrant environment and dynamic atmosphere provide ideal conditions for various activities in a stunning, energetic setting."]},{"heading":"Magnificent House Reef Snorkeling","paragraphs":["Explore the vibrant house reef directly from the beach, featuring colorful corals, tropical fish, and excellent underwater visibility in magnificent waters."]},{"heading":"Scuba Diving Excursions","paragraphs":["Discover nearby stunning dive sites with professional dive operators offering guided dives and certification courses in magnificent marine environments."]},{"heading":"Island Hopping Adventures","paragraphs":["Visit nearby islands, stunning sandbanks, and discover the natural beauty of Vaavu Atoll with vibrant exploration opportunities."]},{"heading":"Traditional Fishing","paragraphs":["Experience authentic Maldivian fishing techniques with local fishermen during sunset and night fishing trips in magnificent community settings."]},{"heading":"Dynamic Cultural Immersion","paragraphs":["Learn about local traditions, participate in community activities, and experience magnificent Maldivian island life with vibrant cultural exchanges."]},{"heading":"Sunset Cruises","paragraphs":["Enjoy stunning sunset cruises around the atoll, often combined with dolphin watching and traditional dhoni sailing in magnificent waters."]},{"heading":"Community Life & Culture","paragraphs":["Felidhoo is home to approximately 2,100 residents who maintain traditional Maldivian ways of life while embracing sustainable tourism. The island''s community is known for their exceptional friendliness, hospitality, and magnificent cultural traditions that create a vibrant atmosphere for visitors."]},{"heading":"Island Life","paragraphs":["Daily life on Felidhoo follows traditional patterns centered around fishing, family, and community activities. The island maintains a magnificent atmosphere where visitors can experience vibrant Maldivian culture and customs in their most dynamic, energetic setting."]},{"heading":"Local Traditions","paragraphs":["The community preserves traditional Maldivian practices including traditional music, dance, handicrafts, and fishing techniques. Visitors can observe and often participate in cultural activities and celebrations in this magnificent island environment."]},{"heading":"Sustainable Tourism","paragraphs":["Felidhoo has embraced sustainable tourism practices that benefit the local community while preserving the island''s natural environment and magnificent cultural heritage for future generations to experience and enjoy."]}],"island_faqs":[{"question":"How do I get to Felidhoo Island?","answer":"Felidhoo Island can be reached by speedboat from Male (1 hour 45 minutes) or by seaplane (25 minutes, weather dependent). Regular ferry services are also available from Male and nearby islands in Vaavu Atoll."},{"question":"What is the best time to visit Felidhoo?","answer":"The best time to visit Felidhoo is during the dry season from December to April when weather conditions are most favorable for beach activities and water sports. However, the island can be visited year-round with the wet season offering fewer crowds and a more magnificent local atmosphere."},{"question":"What accommodation options are available on Felidhoo?","answer":"Felidhoo offers various accommodations including magnificent guesthouses and beachfront properties. Most accommodations offer air conditioning, private bathrooms, and meal packages in a vibrant setting."},{"question":"What makes Felidhoo''s vibrancy special?","answer":"Felidhoo is known for its magnificent and vibrant natural environment. The island maintains traditional Maldivian cultural practices while offering a dynamic atmosphere perfect for energetic exploration. Visitors can experience exciting cultural exchanges and participate in magnificent community activities."}],"island_nearby_slugs":["keyodhoo","thinadhoo","rakeedhoo","fulidhoo"]}'::jsonb
where node_type = 'location' and slug = 'felidhoo';


-- fenfushi
update nodes set attributes = coalesce(attributes, '{}'::jsonb) || '{"island_content_source":"legacy_mtg_guide","island_quick_facts":[],"island_overview":[],"island_sections":[],"island_faqs":[{"question":"What is the best time to visit Fenfushi for surfing?","answer":"The best time for surfing in Fenfushi is during the southwest monsoon (May-October), with peak conditions from June to September. During this period, consistent swells arrive from the southern Indian Ocean, creating ideal surf conditions. The largest and most consistent waves typically occur in July and August. Shoulder seasons (May and October) still offer good waves with fewer crowds. Outside of surf season (November-April), waves are smaller and less consistent but can still be fun for beginners or those looking for a more relaxed surfing experience. For more information about Maldives weather patterns, see our Maldives Weather Guide."},{"question":"Do I need to bring my own surfboard to Fenfushi?","answer":"While bringing your own board is ideal if you have specific preferences, Fenfushi does offer basic surfboard rentals through guesthouses and surf shops. Rental options are typically limited to standard shortboards and funboards (around 6''0\" to 7''0\") in reasonable but not perfect condition. If you''re particular about your equipment or need a specific type of board (like a longboard or step-up), bringing your own is recommended. Some guesthouses offer board storage for returning visitors. For serious surfers, consider bringing essential repair materials as well. If you''re traveling with multiple boards, check with your airline about sports equipment policies."},{"question":"What makes Fenfushi different from other surf destinations in the Maldives?","answer":"Fenfushi stands out from other Maldivian surf destinations in several ways. First, it offers a more authentic local island experience compared to resort-based surf camps, allowing visitors to immerse themselves in Maldivian culture. Second, the island is famous for its traditional boat building heritage, which is unique to this area. Third, Fenfushi''s surf breaks are less crowded than more commercialized spots, offering a more relaxed atmosphere in the lineup. Additionally, the island''s small size creates a tight-knit surf community where visitors can easily connect with locals and other travelers. Unlike resort islands, Fenfushi provides opportunities to experience genuine Maldivian life while still accessing world-class waves. For comparisons with other surf spots, check our Maldives Surfing Guide."},{"question":"Are there non-surfing activities available on Fenfushi?","answer":"Absolutely! While Fenfushi is best known for surfing, there are plenty of other activities for non-surfers or for when the surf is flat. The island offers excellent snorkeling right off the beach, with vibrant coral reefs teeming with marine life. Cultural experiences include visiting the boat building yards, watching traditional Boduberu drum performances, and exploring the island''s coral stone architecture. Fishing trips, sandbank excursions, and island hopping tours are also popular. The island has beautiful beaches for relaxing, and visitors can enjoy authentic Maldivian cuisine at local cafes. For those interested in diving, several nearby dive sites can be arranged through local operators. Check out our Things to Do in Maldives article for more activity ideas."},{"question":"What should I pack for a trip to Fenfushi?","answer":"Packing for Fenfushi requires consideration of both the tropical climate and local customs. Essential items include: surf gear (if not renting), reef-safe sunscreen, rash guard or surf shirt, hat and sunglasses, lightweight clothing that covers shoulders and knees for village wear, swimwear for the designated bikini beach, sandals or flip flops, basic first aid kit, waterproof bag for boat trips, and a reusable water bottle. For electronics, bring waterproof cases, extra memory cards, and universal adapters (Maldives uses UK-style plugs). Mosquito repellent and after-bite cream are recommended. If visiting mosques, women should pack a light scarf. Remember that Fenfushi is a dry island, so don''t bring alcohol. For more packing tips, see our Maldives Packing Guide."}],"island_nearby_slugs":[]}'::jsonb
where node_type = 'location' and slug = 'fenfushi';


-- feridhoo
update nodes set attributes = coalesce(attributes, '{}'::jsonb) || '{"island_content_source":"legacy_mtg_guide","island_quick_facts":[],"island_overview":[],"island_sections":[],"island_faqs":[{"question":"How do I get to Feridhoo Island from Male?","answer":"You can reach Feridhoo Island from Male by public ferry or speedboat. The public ferry operates three times a week (Sunday, Tuesday, and Thursday), departing from Male at 9:00 AM and arriving at Feridhoo around 2:30 PM. Some guesthouses also offer private transfers for a higher fee."},{"question":"What is the best time to visit Feridhoo Island?","answer":"The best time to visit Feridhoo Island is during the dry season from November to April when the weather is sunny with minimal rainfall and calm seas. The peak tourist season is from December to March, offering optimal conditions for beach activities and water sports. The wet season (May to October) sees occasional rain showers and slightly rougher seas, but still has many sunny days and lower prices. For the best balance of good weather and fewer crowds, consider visiting in November or April."},{"question":"Are there any dress code requirements on Feridhoo Island?","answer":"Yes, as Feridhoo is a local inhabited island with a Muslim population, visitors are expected to dress modestly in public areas. Both men and women should cover shoulders and knees when walking around the village, visiting shops, or dining in local restaurants. Swimwear (including bikinis) is only permitted at the designated \"bikini beach\" area. When visiting the mosque or religious sites, women should cover their heads with a scarf. These dress code requirements are a sign of respect for local culture and traditions."},{"question":"Is alcohol available on Feridhoo Island?","answer":"No, alcohol is not available on Feridhoo Island. As a local inhabited island in the Maldives, Feridhoo follows Islamic law which prohibits alcohol. This restriction applies to all local islands in the Maldives. However, if you wish to enjoy alcoholic beverages during your stay, some guesthouses organize day trips to nearby resort islands or uninhabited picnic islands where alcohol is served. Alternatively, you can visit the \"floating bar\" boats that anchor near some local islands, though these are not always available near Feridhoo."},{"question":"What activities are available on Feridhoo Island?","answer":"Feridhoo Island offers a variety of activities for visitors including snorkeling on the house reef, cultural village tours, traditional fishing trips, dolphin watching excursions, island hopping to nearby islands, sandbank picnics, and day trips to luxury resorts. Water sports like kayaking and paddleboarding are available through some guesthouses. Cultural experiences include Boduberu (traditional drumming) performances, handicraft demonstrations, and cooking classes. Most activities can be arranged through your accommodation or local tour operators on the island."}],"island_nearby_slugs":[]}'::jsonb
where node_type = 'location' and slug = 'feridhoo';


