-- filladhoo
update nodes set attributes = coalesce(attributes, '{}'::jsonb) || '{"island_content_source":"legacy_mtg_guide","island_quick_facts":[],"island_overview":[],"island_sections":[],"island_faqs":[{"question":"How do I get to Filladhoo Island?","answer":"Due to the island''s remote location in the northern atolls, direct public ferry services from Male are limited. Most guesthouses can arrange the complete transfer from Male, including the domestic flight and speedboat connection. When planning your journey, remember that weather conditions can occasionally affect flight schedules in this region, so it''s advisable to allow buffer days in your travel plans. The journey to Filladhoo is part of the adventure, offering beautiful aerial views of the Maldivian atolls during the flight and a chance to experience the stunning blue waters during the speedboat transfer."},{"question":"What makes Filladhoo''s fishing traditions unique in the Maldives?","answer":"Filladhoo''s fishing traditions stand out in the Maldives because the island has preserved many traditional fishing methods that have been practiced for generations. The community continues to use sustainable pole-and-line techniques for tuna fishing, which minimizes bycatch and environmental impact. Night fishing using traditional hand-line methods remains an important practice, with knowledge of the best fishing spots and techniques passed down through families. The island maintains traditional boat building skills, with local craftsmen constructing and maintaining the wooden dhonis (traditional fishing boats) using techniques refined over centuries. Fish processing methods including drying, smoking, and making traditional Maldivian fish products like rihaakuru (fish paste) are still practiced. The community follows seasonal fishing patterns based on monsoon changes and fish migrations, demonstrating deep ecological knowledge. These preserved traditions offer visitors insights into sustainable fishing practices that have allowed Maldivian communities to thrive in harmony with the ocean for generations, providing a glimpse into an authentic way of life that is becoming increasingly rare in more developed parts of the country."},{"question":"What is the best time to visit Filladhoo Island?","answer":"The best time to visit Filladhoo Island is during the northeast monsoon season (December to April), which brings dry, sunny weather with lower humidity and calmer seas. This period is ideal for water activities, with excellent visibility for snorkeling and diving. For those interested in experiencing the island''s fishing traditions, this dry season also coincides with good fishing conditions, making it an excellent time to participate in fishing excursions with locals. The southwest monsoon (May to November) brings occasional rain showers but also lower prices and fewer tourists. This season can still offer good fishing opportunities, though sea conditions may be rougher on some days. Water temperature remains warm (27-30C/80-86F) throughout the year. Due to Filladhoo''s northern location, it may experience slightly different weather patterns than southern atolls, with the possibility of brief rain showers even during the dry season. The shoulder months of November and April often offer a good balance of favorable weather and lower visitor numbers."},{"question":"What type of accommodation can I expect on Filladhoo?","answer":"Accommodation on Filladhoo is limited and simple, reflecting the island''s authentic character and minimal tourism development. The island offers a small number of family-run guesthouses that provide clean, comfortable rooms with basic amenities including air conditioning, private bathrooms with hot water, and Wi-Fi (though connectivity may be inconsistent). Most accommodations offer full-board packages that include three home-cooked Maldivian meals daily, featuring fresh seafood caught by local fishermen. Some fishing families also offer homestay experiences where guests stay in a room within a family home, providing deeper cultural immersion and the opportunity to participate in fishing activities. Luxury amenities are limited, and the focus is on authentic experiences rather than high-end facilities. What these accommodations lack in luxury, they make up for in personal service, cultural insights, and genuine hospitality. Visitors should adjust their expectations accordingly and embrace the opportunity to experience authentic island life rather than expecting resort-style amenities."},{"question":"Can I participate in fishing activities as a visitor to Filladhoo?","answer":"Yes, visitors to Filladhoo have excellent opportunities to participate in traditional fishing activities, which is one of the island''s unique attractions. Most guesthouses can arrange for guests to join local fishermen on various fishing excursions, from morning tuna fishing trips to evening reef fishing and night fishing experiences. Traditional pole-and-line tuna fishing demonstrations allow you to learn about and try this sustainable fishing method that has been practiced for generations. Hand-line reef fishing trips provide opportunities to catch various reef fish species while learning about local fishing grounds and techniques. Night fishing excursions are particularly popular, where you can fish under the stars using traditional methods while enjoying the peaceful evening atmosphere. Some accommodations offer more immersive experiences where visitors can participate in the entire process from catching fish to preparing and cooking them for meals. These activities provide not just entertainment but educational insights into sustainable fishing practices and maritime traditions. The level of participation can be adjusted based on your interest and experience, from simple observation to active involvement. Participating in these activities provides a unique experience not commonly available on other Maldivian islands while supporting the local fishing community."}],"island_nearby_slugs":[]}'::jsonb
where node_type = 'location' and slug = 'filladhoo';


-- finey
update nodes set attributes = coalesce(attributes, '{}'::jsonb) || '{"island_content_source":"legacy_mtg_guide","island_quick_facts":[],"island_overview":[],"island_sections":[],"island_faqs":[{"question":"How do I get to Finey Island?","answer":"Due to the island''s remote location in the northern atolls, direct public ferry services from Male are limited. Most guesthouses can arrange the complete transfer from Male, including the domestic flight and speedboat connection. When planning your journey, remember that weather conditions can occasionally affect flight schedules in this region, so it''s advisable to allow buffer days in your travel plans. The journey to Finey is part of the adventure, offering beautiful aerial views of the Maldivian atolls during the flight and a chance to experience the stunning blue waters during the speedboat transfer."},{"question":"What makes Finey''s healing traditions unique in the Maldives?","answer":"Finey''s healing traditions stand out in the Maldives because the island has preserved a comprehensive system of traditional medicine that combines various influences while maintaining distinctly Maldivian characteristics. The island is known for its traditional healers (hakims) who practice diagnostic methods such as pulse reading and observation techniques that have been refined over generations. Finey''s healers maintain extensive knowledge of local medicinal plants and their applications, with some families specializing in specific types of treatments or conditions. The island has preserved traditional preparation methods for herbal remedies, including decoctions, infusions, poultices, and medicated oils that are created using precise techniques. What makes Finey special is the integration of Islamic healing traditions with pre-Islamic practices that have been adapted over centuries, creating a unique synthesis of spiritual and physical healing approaches. The community maintains specialized therapeutic massage techniques that differ from those found in other parts of the Maldives, with specific methods for different conditions. Finey is also known for its cultivation of medicinal plants, with some families maintaining gardens specifically for healing purposes, preserving plant varieties that have become rare elsewhere. These preserved traditions offer visitors insights into a holistic approach to health and well-being that differs from modern medicine while complementing it, providing a cultural experience that connects to centuries of Maldivian healing wisdom."},{"question":"What is the best time to visit Finey Island?","answer":"The best time to visit Finey Island is during the northeast monsoon season (December to April), which brings dry, sunny weather with lower humidity and calmer seas. This period is ideal for water activities, with excellent visibility for snorkeling and diving. For those interested in experiencing the island''s healing traditions, this dry season is also excellent as many medicinal plants are in bloom or fruit, and outdoor wellness activities can be conducted without interruption from rain. The southwest monsoon (May to November) brings occasional rain showers but also lower prices and fewer tourists. This season can be interesting for those interested in medicinal plants, as the increased rainfall supports lush growth, though some outdoor activities may be affected by rain. Water temperature remains warm (27-30C/80-86F) throughout the year. Due to Finey''s northern location, it may experience slightly different weather patterns than southern atolls, with the possibility of brief rain showers even during the dry season. The shoulder months of November and April often offer a good balance of favorable weather and lower visitor numbers."},{"question":"What type of accommodation can I expect on Finey?","answer":"Accommodation on Finey is limited and simple, reflecting the island''s authentic character and minimal tourism development. The island offers a small number of family-run guesthouses that provide clean, comfortable rooms with basic amenities including air conditioning, private bathrooms with hot water, and Wi-Fi (though connectivity may be inconsistent). Most accommodations offer full-board packages that include three home-cooked Maldivian meals daily, featuring fresh seafood caught by local fishermen and sometimes incorporating local medicinal herbs in the cuisine. Some healing families also offer homestay experiences where guests stay in a room within a family home, providing deeper cultural immersion and the opportunity to learn about traditional medicine. A few properties are located near the beach, offering easy access to the island''s beautiful shores. Luxury amenities are limited, and the focus is on authentic experiences rather than high-end facilities. What these accommodations lack in luxury, they make up for in personal service, cultural insights, and genuine hospitality. Visitors should adjust their expectations accordingly and embrace the opportunity to experience authentic island life rather than expecting resort-style amenities."},{"question":"Can I experience traditional healing practices as a visitor to Finey?","answer":"Yes, visitors to Finey have excellent opportunities to experience traditional healing practices, which is one of the island''s unique attractions. Most guesthouses can arrange for guests to participate in various wellness experiences led by local healers. These may include consultations with traditional healers who can provide insights into Maldivian approaches to health and well-being. Medicinal plant walks allow visitors to learn about the various healing plants that grow on the island, their identification, and their traditional uses. Herbal preparation demonstrations show how medicinal plants are processed into remedies, from simple teas to more complex formulations. Some healers offer traditional massage sessions that incorporate local techniques and medicinal oils. Wellness workshops provide hands-on experience in creating simple remedies that visitors can learn to make themselves. For those with specific health interests, specialized sessions focusing on particular aspects of traditional medicine can sometimes be arranged. These experiences provide not just entertainment but educational insights into a holistic approach to health that has supported island communities for centuries. The level of participation can be adjusted based on your interest and comfort level, from simple observation to more immersive experiences. It''s important to note that these traditional practices are offered as cultural experiences and complement rather than replace modern medical care."}],"island_nearby_slugs":[]}'::jsonb
where node_type = 'location' and slug = 'finey';


-- fiyoari
update nodes set attributes = coalesce(attributes, '{}'::jsonb) || '{"island_content_source":"legacy_mtg_guide","island_quick_facts":[],"island_overview":[],"island_sections":[],"island_faqs":[{"question":"How do I get to Faresmaathodaa Island?","answer":"Public ferry service operates weekly from Male (approximately 18-20 hours journey time). Private speedboat transfers can be arranged through guesthouses (approximately 7.5 hours from Male)."},{"question":"What is the best time to visit Faresmaathodaa Island?","answer":"The best time to visit Faresmaathodaa Island is during the northeast monsoon season (December to April), which brings dry, sunny weather with lower humidity and calmer seas. For whale shark encounters, visit during the southwest monsoon (May to December). Water temperature remains warm (27-30C/80-86F) throughout the year."},{"question":"What makes Faresmaathodaa different from other local islands in the Maldives?","answer":"Faresmaathodaa stands out for its exceptional preservation of traditional Maldivian life in a remote setting and its unique twin-island structure. Unlike most Maldivian islands, Faresmaathodaa consists of two separate islands connected by a small bridge, creating a distinctive figure-eight shape. This unique geography provides additional shoreline and beach access, while the channel between the islands creates a natural harbor and a special marine environment."},{"question":"Can I walk between the two parts of Faresmaathodaa Island?","answer":"Yes, the two parts of Faresmaathodaa Island are connected by a small bridge that allows easy pedestrian access between them. Walking across this bridge is actually a popular activity for visitors, as it offers excellent views of the channel and surrounding waters. The bridge has become a gathering spot for locals and visitors alike, especially during sunset when the views are particularly spectacular."},{"question":"What marine life can I expect to see while snorkeling around Faresmaathodaa?","answer":"Faresmaathodaa''s waters offer excellent marine biodiversity, including healthy coral formations with both hard and soft corals. Common sightings include reef sharks (particularly blacktip and whitetip), sea turtles, various ray species, and abundant reef fish. The channel between the two parts of the island creates a unique marine environment with different currents and marine life. Seasonal visitors include whale sharks (May-December) and manta rays. The house reef provides easy access to this underwater world directly from shore."}],"island_nearby_slugs":[]}'::jsonb
where node_type = 'location' and slug = 'fiyoari';


-- foakaidhoo
update nodes set attributes = coalesce(attributes, '{}'::jsonb) || '{"island_content_source":"legacy_mtg_guide","island_quick_facts":[{"label":"Location","value":"Shaviyani Atoll, Northern Maldives"},{"label":"Island Type","value":"Inhabited Local Island"},{"label":"Population","value":"Approximately 1,200 residents"},{"label":"Size","value":"1.3 km long, 0.8 km wide"},{"label":"Distance from Male","value":"210 km"},{"label":"Transfer Options","value":"Seaplane or domestic flight + speedboat"},{"label":"Known For","value":"Stunning culture, pristine beaches, exceptional traditions"},{"label":"Best For","value":"Culture enthusiasts, beach lovers, tradition seekers, nature lovers"}],"island_overview":["Foakaidhoo Island is a stunning local island in Shaviyani Atoll that offers visitors an exceptional glimpse into traditional Maldivian life in the northern region of the archipelago. This pristine island combines natural beauty with a remarkable atmosphere, providing an ideal destination for travelers seeking extraordinary cultural experiences and stunning tropical surroundings.","Known for its pristine beaches, stunning coral reefs, and exceptional marine biodiversity, Foakaidhoo provides remarkable opportunities for snorkeling, swimming, and underwater exploration. The island''s exceptional community embraces visitors with traditional Maldivian warmth and shares their remarkable way of life with stunning hospitality.","What makes Foakaidhoo special is its stunning natural environment and exceptional northern location. Visitors can enjoy pristine beaches, explore rich marine ecosystems, and experience remarkable island culture while staying in comfortable accommodations that showcase the stunning Maldivian lifestyle."],"island_sections":[{"heading":"Location & Map","paragraphs":["Foakaidhoo Island is stunningly located in the northern part of Shaviyani Atoll, approximately 210 kilometers from Male. This location provides a stunning and exceptional experience in the northern Maldives, while maintaining remarkable accessibility through seaplane transfers or domestic flights.","The island''s position offers exceptional protection from strong currents while providing access to pristine coral reefs and diverse marine ecosystems. Its location in the atoll makes it an ideal base for exploring the natural beauty and cultural richness of Shaviyani Atoll in its most stunning form."]},{"heading":"Foakaidhoo: Stunning Paradise & Marine Excellence","paragraphs":["Foakaidhoo Island is blessed with exceptional natural beauty, featuring pristine white sand beaches, crystal-clear turquoise waters, and one of the most stunning marine environments in Shaviyani Atoll. The island offers perfect conditions for beach relaxation and marine exploration in an exceptional, remarkable setting."]},{"heading":"Pristine White Sand Beaches","paragraphs":["Foakaidhoo features stunning white sand beaches with gentle slopes and calm waters, perfect for swimming, sunbathing, and exceptional beach activities."]},{"heading":"Stunning House Reef Snorkeling","paragraphs":["The island''s house reef is easily accessible from the beach and offers exceptional snorkeling with diverse marine life and colorful coral formations."]},{"heading":"Exceptional Island Community","paragraphs":["Experience the remarkable spirit of traditional northern island life with friendly locals and stunning Maldivian culture in an exceptional community setting."]},{"heading":"Remarkable Traditional Heritage","paragraphs":["Discover the island''s rich traditional practices and learn about cultural customs that make this community stunning in the northern Maldives."]},{"heading":"Beach Features","paragraphs":["Foakaidhoo''s coastal highlights include:"]},{"heading":"Marine Environment","paragraphs":["The waters around Foakaidhoo feature:"]},{"heading":"Activities & Experiences","paragraphs":["Foakaidhoo offers a perfect blend of marine adventures, cultural experiences, and stunning activities. The island''s exceptional environment and remarkable atmosphere provide ideal conditions for various activities in a pristine, extraordinary setting."]},{"heading":"Stunning House Reef Snorkeling","paragraphs":["Explore the exceptional house reef directly from the beach, featuring colorful corals, tropical fish, and remarkable underwater visibility in stunning waters."]},{"heading":"Scuba Diving Excursions","paragraphs":["Discover nearby pristine dive sites with professional dive operators offering guided dives and certification courses in stunning marine environments."]},{"heading":"Island Hopping Adventures","paragraphs":["Visit nearby islands, pristine sandbanks, and discover the natural beauty of Shaviyani Atoll with exceptional exploration opportunities."]},{"heading":"Traditional Fishing","paragraphs":["Experience authentic Maldivian fishing techniques with local fishermen during sunset and night fishing trips in stunning community settings."]},{"heading":"Remarkable Cultural Immersion","paragraphs":["Learn about local traditions, participate in community activities, and experience stunning Maldivian island life with exceptional cultural exchanges."]},{"heading":"Sunset Cruises","paragraphs":["Enjoy pristine sunset cruises around the atoll, often combined with dolphin watching and traditional dhoni sailing in stunning waters."]},{"heading":"Community Life & Culture","paragraphs":["Foakaidhoo is home to approximately 1,200 residents who maintain traditional Maldivian ways of life while embracing sustainable tourism. The island''s community is known for their exceptional friendliness, hospitality, and stunning cultural traditions that create an exceptional atmosphere for visitors."]},{"heading":"Island Life","paragraphs":["Daily life on Foakaidhoo follows traditional patterns centered around fishing, culture, and community activities. The island maintains a stunning atmosphere where visitors can experience exceptional Maldivian culture and customs in their most remarkable, extraordinary setting."]},{"heading":"Local Traditions","paragraphs":["The community preserves traditional Maldivian practices including traditional music, dance, handicrafts, and cultural techniques. Visitors can observe and often participate in cultural activities and celebrations in this stunning island environment."]},{"heading":"Sustainable Tourism","paragraphs":["Foakaidhoo has embraced sustainable tourism practices that benefit the local community while preserving the island''s natural environment and stunning cultural heritage for future generations to experience and enjoy."]}],"island_faqs":[{"question":"How do I get to Foakaidhoo Island?","answer":"Regular inter-island ferry services are also available between Shaviyani Atoll islands."},{"question":"What is the best time to visit Foakaidhoo?","answer":"The best time to visit Foakaidhoo is during the dry season from December to April when weather conditions are most favorable for beach activities and water sports. However, the island can be visited year-round with the wet season offering fewer crowds and a more stunning local atmosphere."},{"question":"What accommodation options are available on Foakaidhoo?","answer":"Foakaidhoo offers various accommodations including stunning guesthouses and beachfront properties. Most accommodations offer air conditioning, private bathrooms, and meal packages in an exceptional setting."},{"question":"What makes Foakaidhoo''s culture special?","answer":"Foakaidhoo is known for its stunning and exceptional cultural environment in the northern Maldives. The island maintains traditional Maldivian cultural practices while offering a remarkable atmosphere perfect for extraordinary exploration. Visitors can experience pristine cultural exchanges and participate in stunning community activities."}],"island_nearby_slugs":["feydhoo","feevah","bileffahi","noomaraa","narudhoo","milandhoo","maroshi","maaungoodhoo","lhaimagu","komandoo","kanditheemu","goidhoo","funadhoo"]}'::jsonb
where node_type = 'location' and slug = 'foakaidhoo';


-- foddhoo
update nodes set attributes = coalesce(attributes, '{}'::jsonb) || '{"island_content_source":"legacy_mtg_guide","island_quick_facts":[{"label":"Location","value":"Noonu Atoll, Northern Maldives"},{"label":"Island Type","value":"Inhabited Local Island"},{"label":"Population","value":"Approximately 600 residents"},{"label":"Size","value":"0.7 km long, 0.4 km wide"},{"label":"Distance from Male","value":"180 km"},{"label":"Transfer Options","value":"Seaplane or domestic flight + speedboat"},{"label":"Known For","value":"Pristine beaches, excellent snorkeling, peaceful atmosphere"},{"label":"Best For","value":"Nature lovers, snorkelers, cultural travelers, budget travelers"}],"island_overview":["Nestled in the pristine waters of Noonu Atoll, Fodhdhoo Island represents the essence of authentic Maldivian island life. This charming local island offers visitors a unique opportunity to experience traditional culture while enjoying some of the most beautiful beaches in the northern Maldives.","Fodhdhoo stands out for its untouched natural beauty, crystal-clear lagoons, and vibrant house reef that''s perfect for snorkeling. The island maintains its traditional character while welcoming visitors with genuine Maldivian hospitality and warmth.","What makes Fodhdhoo truly special is its peaceful atmosphere, excellent marine life, and the opportunity to experience authentic island culture. Visitors can enjoy budget-friendly accommodations, delicious local cuisine, and unforgettable underwater adventures."],"island_sections":[{"heading":"Location & Map","paragraphs":["Fodhdhoo Island is strategically located in the central part of Noonu Atoll, approximately 180 kilometers from Male. This location ensures an authentic and peaceful experience while still offering excellent accessibility to the capital and international airport.","The island''s position provides natural protection from strong currents while maintaining access to some of the best snorkeling and diving sites in the Maldives. The surrounding waters feature healthy coral reefs and abundant marine life."]},{"heading":"Fodhdhoo: Natural Beauty & Marine Wonders","paragraphs":["Fodhdhoo Island is renowned for its exceptional natural beauty, featuring powder-white sand beaches, crystal-clear turquoise waters, and one of the most vibrant house reefs in Noonu Atoll. The island offers an unspoiled tropical paradise perfect for relaxation and marine exploration."]},{"heading":"Pristine White Sand Beaches","paragraphs":["Fodhdhoo boasts some of the most beautiful beaches in Noonu Atoll, with soft white sand and crystal-clear waters perfect for swimming and sunbathing."]},{"heading":"World-Class Snorkeling","paragraphs":["The island''s house reef is easily accessible from the beach and features diverse marine life, colorful corals, and excellent underwater visibility."]},{"heading":"Authentic Island Culture","paragraphs":["Experience genuine Maldivian hospitality and traditional island life in a peaceful setting away from commercial tourism."]},{"heading":"Pristine Sandbank Visits","paragraphs":["Explore nearby uninhabited sandbanks for the ultimate desert island experience with picnics and swimming in crystal-clear waters."]},{"heading":"Beach Highlights","paragraphs":["Fodhdhoo''s coastal features include:"]},{"heading":"Marine Environment","paragraphs":["The island''s underwater world features:"]},{"heading":"Activities & Experiences","paragraphs":["Fodhdhoo offers an excellent variety of activities focused on marine adventures, cultural experiences, and natural exploration. The island''s pristine environment provides perfect opportunities for both adventure and relaxation."]},{"heading":"House Reef Snorkeling","paragraphs":["Explore the vibrant house reef directly from the beach, featuring colorful corals, tropical fish, and excellent underwater visibility."]},{"heading":"Scuba Diving Adventures","paragraphs":["Discover world-class dive sites around Noonu Atoll with professional dive operators offering courses and guided dives."]},{"heading":"Island Hopping Tours","paragraphs":["Visit nearby islands and discover uninhabited sandbanks, each offering unique experiences and pristine natural beauty."]},{"heading":"Traditional Night Fishing","paragraphs":["Join local fishermen for authentic night fishing experiences using traditional hand lines under the starlit Maldivian sky."]},{"heading":"Cultural Experiences","paragraphs":["Immerse yourself in local community life, learn traditional crafts, and experience authentic Maldivian customs and traditions."]},{"heading":"Sunset Cruises","paragraphs":["Enjoy magical sunset cruises around the atoll, often combined with dolphin watching and traditional dhoni sailing."]},{"heading":"People & Community Life","paragraphs":["Fodhdhoo is home to a close-knit community of approximately 600 residents who have preserved traditional Maldivian ways of life for generations. The island''s population is renowned for their warmth, hospitality, and strong community bonds."]},{"heading":"Daily Life","paragraphs":["Life on Fodhdhoo follows the natural rhythms of island living, beginning with morning prayers and continuing with fishing, community work, and family activities. The island maintains a peaceful, unhurried pace that reflects traditional Maldivian values."]},{"heading":"Culture & Traditions","paragraphs":["Fodhdhoo preserves authentic Maldivian cultural traditions including traditional music, dance, and handicrafts. The community celebrates Islamic festivals with enthusiasm and maintains traditional practices such as dhoni building and traditional fishing techniques."]},{"heading":"Local Economy","paragraphs":["The island''s economy is primarily based on fishing and increasingly tourism. Many families engage in traditional occupations while also participating in the growing tourism sector through guesthouses, restaurants, and tour services."]}],"island_faqs":[{"question":"How do I get to Fodhdhoo Island?","answer":"Regular ferry services are also available from Male and nearby islands in Noonu Atoll."},{"question":"What is the best time to visit Fodhdhoo?","answer":"The best time to visit Fodhdhoo is during the dry season from December to April when weather conditions are most favorable. However, the island can be visited year-round, with the wet season (May-November) offering fewer crowds and lower accommodation rates."},{"question":"What accommodation options are available on Fodhdhoo?","answer":"Fodhdhoo offers various budget-friendly and mid-range accommodations including family guesthouses and beachfront properties. Most accommodations offer air conditioning, private bathrooms, and meal packages."},{"question":"What activities are available on Fodhdhoo?","answer":"Fodhdhoo offers excellent snorkeling from the house reef, diving excursions, island hopping tours, cultural experiences, traditional fishing trips, and sunset cruises. The island is particularly known for its pristine marine environment and authentic cultural experiences."}],"island_nearby_slugs":["manadhoo","velidhoo","miladhoo","maafaru","landhoo","kendhikolhudhoo","magoodhoo","henbandhoo","kudafaree","lhohi","maalhendhoo"]}'::jsonb
where node_type = 'location' and slug = 'foddhoo';


-- fonadhoo
update nodes set attributes = coalesce(attributes, '{}'::jsonb) || '{"island_content_source":"legacy_mtg_guide","island_quick_facts":[{"label":"Location","value":"Laamu Atoll, Southern Maldives"},{"label":"Island Type","value":"Inhabited Local Island"},{"label":"Population","value":"Approximately 1,200 residents"},{"label":"Size","value":"1.2 km long, 0.5 km wide"},{"label":"Distance from Male","value":"240 km"},{"label":"Transfer Options","value":"Domestic flight + ferry"},{"label":"Known For","value":"Authentic culture, beautiful beaches, peacefulness"},{"label":"Best For","value":"Cultural travelers, budget travelers, snorkelers"}],"island_overview":["Located in the southern Laamu Atoll, Fonadhoo Island offers visitors an authentic Maldivian experience away from the crowds. This tranquil island maintains its traditional character while providing comfortable facilities for tourists seeking cultural immersion in the Maldives.","What makes Fonadhoo special is its peaceful atmosphere, beautiful beaches, and rich cultural heritage. The island features powdery white sand beaches, crystal-clear turquoise waters, and a vibrant local community that welcomes visitors with warm hospitality.","Visitors to Fonadhoo are drawn by its authentic island life, excellent snorkeling opportunities, cultural experiences, and budget-friendly accommodations. The island''s remote location provides a true escape from modern life while still offering comfortable amenities."],"island_sections":[{"heading":"Location & Map","paragraphs":["Fonadhoo Island is situated in the southern part of Laamu Atoll, approximately 240 kilometers from Male. This remote location provides an authentic Maldivian experience away from the more touristy areas, with stunning natural beauty and traditional island life.","The island''s position offers protection from strong currents while still providing access to excellent snorkeling and diving sites. The surrounding waters feature healthy coral reefs and abundant marine life, making it a great destination for underwater exploration."]},{"heading":"Fonadhoo: Natural Beauty & Beaches","paragraphs":["Fonadhoo Island is renowned for its pristine beaches and natural beauty, featuring white sand shores and healthy coral reefs. The island offers visitors a peaceful tropical paradise with excellent snorkeling and relaxation opportunities."]},{"heading":"Beautiful White Sand Beaches","paragraphs":["The island features stunning white sand beaches with crystal-clear turquoise waters, offering the perfect setting for relaxation and sunbathing."]},{"heading":"Excellent Snorkeling","paragraphs":["Explore the vibrant house reef accessible from shore, featuring diverse marine life and coral formations perfect for snorkeling."]},{"heading":"Authentic Island Life","paragraphs":["Experience traditional Maldivian culture and hospitality in a peaceful setting away from tourist crowds."]},{"heading":"Sandbank Excursions","paragraphs":["Visit pristine uninhabited sandbanks for picnics, swimming, and the ultimate desert island experience."]},{"heading":"Beach Highlights","paragraphs":["Fonadhoo''s beaches offer:"]},{"heading":"Marine Environment","paragraphs":["The island''s marine ecosystem features:"]},{"heading":"Activities & Experiences","paragraphs":["Fonadhoo offers a variety of activities focused on marine adventures, cultural experiences, and relaxation. The island''s peaceful environment provides excellent opportunities for both adventure and tranquility."]},{"heading":"Snorkeling","paragraphs":["Explore the vibrant house reef directly from shore or join boat excursions to nearby coral gardens and marine sanctuaries."]},{"heading":"Scuba Diving","paragraphs":["Discover underwater wonders at nearby dive sites with professional dive operators offering courses and guided dives."]},{"heading":"Sandbank Visits","paragraphs":["Experience pristine uninhabited sandbanks for picnics, swimming, and the ultimate desert island adventure."]},{"heading":"Traditional Fishing","paragraphs":["Join local fishermen for traditional night fishing experiences using hand lines under the starlit sky."]},{"heading":"Cultural Experiences","paragraphs":["Engage with local community life, learn traditional crafts, and experience authentic Maldivian hospitality."]},{"heading":"Beach Relaxation","paragraphs":["Enjoy the pristine beaches, perfect for sunbathing, reading, and enjoying the peaceful island atmosphere."]},{"heading":"People & Community Life","paragraphs":["Fonadhoo is home to a peaceful community of approximately 1,200 residents who maintain traditional Maldivian ways of life. The island''s population is known for their exceptional hospitality, strong community bonds, and welcoming attitude toward visitors."]},{"heading":"Daily Life","paragraphs":["Life on Fonadhoo follows traditional Maldivian rhythms, beginning with morning prayers and continuing with fishing, tourism-related work, and community activities. The island maintains a relaxed atmosphere where traditional values are preserved."]},{"heading":"Culture & Traditions","paragraphs":["Fonadhoo preserves authentic Maldivian cultural traditions including traditional music, dance, and crafts. The community celebrates Islamic festivals with enthusiasm and maintains traditional practices such as boat building, fishing techniques, and local cuisine preparation."]},{"heading":"Local Economy","paragraphs":["The island''s economy is based on fishing, agriculture, and increasingly tourism. Many families engage in traditional occupations while also participating in the growing tourism sector through guesthouses, restaurants, and tour services."]}],"island_faqs":[{"question":"How do I get to Fonadhoo Island?","answer":"Fonadhoo Island can be reached by domestic flight to Kadhdhoo Airport (1 hour from Male) followed by a 30-minute ferry ride. Direct seaplane transfers from Male are also available but more expensive. There is also a weekly public ferry from Male that takes 14-16 hours."},{"question":"What is the best time to visit Fonadhoo?","answer":"The best time to visit Fonadhoo is during the dry season from December to April when the weather is sunny and rainfall is minimal. However, the island can be visited year-round, with the wet season (May-November) offering fewer crowds and lower prices."},{"question":"What accommodation options are available on Fonadhoo?","answer":"Fonadhoo offers various budget-friendly and mid-range accommodations including family-run guesthouses and beachfront properties. Most accommodations offer air conditioning, private bathrooms, and meal packages."},{"question":"What activities are available on Fonadhoo?","answer":"Fonadhoo offers excellent snorkeling, diving opportunities, sandbank excursions, cultural experiences, and beach relaxation. Many guesthouses can arrange fishing trips, island hopping tours, and visits to nearby uninhabited islands."}],"island_nearby_slugs":["gan","maabaidhoo","mundoo","isdhoo","kunahandhoo","dhanbidhoo","hithadhoo","maamendhoo","maavah"]}'::jsonb
where node_type = 'location' and slug = 'fonadhoo';


-- fulhadhoo
update nodes set attributes = coalesce(attributes, '{}'::jsonb) || '{"island_content_source":"legacy_mtg_guide","island_quick_facts":[],"island_overview":[],"island_sections":[],"island_faqs":[{"question":"How do I get to Fulhadhoo Island?","answer":"Fulhadhoo Island is accessible via several transportation options, though its more remote location makes the journey slightly more complex than to some other islands. The most economical route is by public ferry from Male, which operates twice a week (Monday and Thursday), departing at 8:30 AM and arriving at Fulhadhoo around 4:00 PM. The most convenient but expensive option is to take a domestic flight from Velana International Airport to Dharavandhoo Airport (approximately 30 minutes), followed by a speedboat to Fulhadhoo (around 45 minutes). Another option is to travel to Eydhafushi (the atoll capital) first, then arrange a local boat transfer to Fulhadhoo. Most guesthouses on Fulhadhoo can arrange transfers and will provide detailed information about the best options based on your arrival date and preferences. Due to the island''s remote location, it''s essential to plan transportation well in advance."},{"question":"What is the best time to visit Fulhadhoo Island?","answer":"The best time to visit Fulhadhoo Island depends on your priorities. For beach activities and optimal weather conditions, the northeast monsoon season (November to April) brings dry, sunny weather with lower humidity and calmer seas. This period is ideal for beach relaxation, snorkeling, and island exploration, with January to March typically offering the most reliable weather conditions with minimal rainfall and gentle sea breezes. If you''re specifically interested in manta ray and whale shark encounters at nearby Hanifaru Bay, plan your visit between May and November, with peak season being June to October when plankton concentrations attract these magnificent creatures. This coincides with the southwest monsoon season, which brings occasional rain showers and slightly rougher seas, though there are still many sunny days. For the best balance of good weather and marine life encounters, consider visiting during the transitional months of April-May or October-November when you might experience the benefits of both seasons. Water temperature remains warm (27-30C/80-86F) throughout the year, making Fulhadhoo a viable destination in any season depending on your preferences."},{"question":"What makes Fulhadhoo different from other local islands in the Maldives?","answer":"Fulhadhoo distinguishes itself from other local islands through several unique characteristics. First and foremost are its extraordinary beaches, which many visitors consider among the most beautiful in the entire Maldives, rivaling or exceeding those of luxury resorts. The western beach in particular stretches for nearly a kilometer with powder-fine white sand and crystal-clear waters in multiple shades of blue. Second is the island''s remarkable seclusion and minimal development. With only about 250 residents and very limited tourism infrastructure, Fulhadhoo offers a level of tranquility and privacy that''s increasingly rare, even on local islands. Visitors often report having entire beaches to themselves. Third is the island''s pristine natural environment, with healthy coral reefs accessible directly from shore and minimal human impact on the surrounding marine ecosystem. Fourth is the authentic cultural experience - due to its small size and relative isolation, Fulhadhoo has preserved traditional Maldivian customs, lifestyle, and community bonds that have evolved or faded on more developed islands. Fifth is the island''s location within the UNESCO Biosphere Reserve, providing access to exceptional marine biodiversity while benefiting from conservation measures. For travelers seeking natural beauty, peace, and authentic experiences rather than modern amenities or nightlife, Fulhadhoo represents one of the last opportunities to experience the Maldives in its most pristine and traditional form."},{"question":"Are there any special considerations for visiting such a remote island?","answer":"Visiting Fulhadhoo requires some special considerations due to its remote location and limited infrastructure. First, plan your transportation carefully, as public ferries only operate twice weekly and private transfers should be arranged well in advance. Second, pack essentials as shopping options are extremely limited - bring any medications, specific toiletries, sunscreen, insect repellent, and other personal necessities you might need. Third, bring sufficient cash as there are no ATMs on the island, and credit cards are rarely accepted. Fourth, prepare for limited connectivity - while mobile signals are available, internet access may be slow and intermittent, making Fulhadhoo perfect for a digital detox. Fifth, adjust your expectations regarding amenities - accommodations are clean and comfortable but basic, with limited hot water and potential power fluctuations. Sixth, respect the conservative local culture by dressing modestly in public areas and observing local customs. Seventh, be self-sufficient in terms of entertainment - bring books, games, or other offline activities as there are no organized entertainment venues. Eighth, consider bringing small gifts for your host family or local children, such as school supplies or practical items. Ninth, pack a good first aid kit as medical facilities are basic. Finally, embrace flexibility and patience - island time moves at a different pace, and weather conditions can affect planned activities. With the right preparation and mindset, these considerations become part of the authentic experience that makes Fulhadhoo so special."},{"question":"What should I pack for a stay on Fulhadhoo Island?","answer":"Packing for Fulhadhoo requires thoughtful preparation due to the island''s remote location and limited shopping options. Essential clothing items include lightweight, breathable fabrics suitable for tropical weather, modest attire for village areas (covering shoulders and knees), swimwear for designated beaches, a light rain jacket or umbrella (especially during the southwest monsoon), and a sun hat and sunglasses for protection. Beach and water essentials should include high-SPF sunscreen (reef-safe preferred), after-sun lotion, a beach towel, water shoes for reef walking, and snorkeling equipment if you have your own (though basic gear can be rented). Health and personal items should include any prescription medications (in original packaging), a comprehensive first aid kit, insect repellent, hand sanitizer, toiletries, and feminine hygiene products. Practical items to consider are a good flashlight or headlamp (essential for evening walks), a reusable water bottle, a dry bag for boat trips, a power bank for electronics, universal power adapters, and a small backpack for day excursions. Entertainment options like books, e-readers, downloaded movies/music, and card games are recommended as there are no entertainment venues. Consider bringing cash in US dollars (widely accepted) as there are no ATMs, and small gifts for hosts or local children such as school supplies. Finally, don''t forget your camera to capture the island''s extraordinary beauty, preferably with underwater capabilities or a waterproof case."}],"island_nearby_slugs":[]}'::jsonb
where node_type = 'location' and slug = 'fulhadhoo';


-- fulidhoo
update nodes set attributes = coalesce(attributes, '{}'::jsonb) || '{"island_content_source":"legacy_mtg_guide","island_quick_facts":[{"label":"Location","value":"Vaavu Atoll, Central Maldives"},{"label":"Island Type","value":"Inhabited Local Island"},{"label":"Population","value":"Approximately 1,800 residents"},{"label":"Size","value":"1.6 km long, 0.9 km wide"},{"label":"Distance from Male","value":"72 km"},{"label":"Transfer Options","value":"Speedboat or seaplane"},{"label":"Known For","value":"Extraordinary culture, breathtaking beaches, excellent snorkeling"},{"label":"Best For","value":"Culture enthusiasts, beach lovers, snorkelers, nature lovers"}],"island_overview":["Fulidhoo Island is an extraordinary local island in Vaavu Atoll that offers visitors a captivating glimpse into traditional Maldivian life. This remarkable island combines natural beauty with an enchanting atmosphere, providing an ideal destination for travelers seeking exceptional cultural experiences and breathtaking tropical surroundings.","Known for its beautiful beaches, extraordinary coral reefs, and excellent marine biodiversity, Fulidhoo provides wonderful opportunities for snorkeling, swimming, and underwater exploration. The island''s captivating community embraces visitors with traditional Maldivian warmth and shares their remarkable way of life with extraordinary hospitality.","What makes Fulidhoo special is its extraordinary natural environment and captivating island setting. Visitors can enjoy breathtaking beaches, explore rich marine ecosystems, and experience enchanting island culture while staying in comfortable accommodations that showcase the extraordinary Maldivian lifestyle."],"island_sections":[{"heading":"Location & Map","paragraphs":["Fulidhoo Island is beautifully located in the heart of Vaavu Atoll, approximately 72 kilometers from Male. This location provides an extraordinary and captivating experience while maintaining excellent accessibility to the capital and international airport through various transfer options.","The island''s position offers excellent protection from strong currents while providing access to breathtaking coral reefs and diverse marine ecosystems. Its location in the atoll makes it an ideal base for exploring the natural beauty and cultural richness of Vaavu Atoll in its most extraordinary form."]},{"heading":"Fulidhoo: Extraordinary Paradise & Marine Enchantment","paragraphs":["Fulidhoo Island is blessed with exceptional natural beauty, featuring breathtaking white sand beaches, crystal-clear turquoise waters, and one of the most extraordinary marine environments in Vaavu Atoll. The island offers perfect conditions for beach relaxation and marine exploration in a captivating, enchanting setting."]},{"heading":"Breathtaking White Sand Beaches","paragraphs":["Fulidhoo features extraordinary white sand beaches with gentle slopes and calm waters, perfect for swimming, sunbathing, and enchanting beach activities."]},{"heading":"Extraordinary House Reef Snorkeling","paragraphs":["The island''s house reef is easily accessible from the beach and offers captivating snorkeling with diverse marine life and colorful coral formations."]},{"heading":"Captivating Island Community","paragraphs":["Experience the enchanting spirit of traditional island life with friendly locals and extraordinary Maldivian culture in a captivating community setting."]},{"heading":"Enchanting Sandbank Adventures","paragraphs":["Explore nearby uninhabited sandbanks and extraordinary islands around Fulidhoo for breathtaking tropical paradise experiences with rich marine life."]},{"heading":"Beach Features","paragraphs":["Fulidhoo''s coastal highlights include:"]},{"heading":"Marine Environment","paragraphs":["The waters around Fulidhoo feature:"]},{"heading":"Activities & Experiences","paragraphs":["Fulidhoo offers a perfect blend of marine adventures, cultural experiences, and extraordinary activities. The island''s captivating environment and enchanting atmosphere provide ideal conditions for various activities in a breathtaking, remarkable setting."]},{"heading":"Extraordinary House Reef Snorkeling","paragraphs":["Explore the captivating house reef directly from the beach, featuring colorful corals, tropical fish, and excellent underwater visibility in extraordinary waters."]},{"heading":"Scuba Diving Excursions","paragraphs":["Discover nearby breathtaking dive sites with professional dive operators offering guided dives and certification courses in extraordinary marine environments."]},{"heading":"Island Hopping Adventures","paragraphs":["Visit nearby islands, breathtaking sandbanks, and discover the natural beauty of Vaavu Atoll with captivating exploration opportunities."]},{"heading":"Traditional Fishing","paragraphs":["Experience authentic Maldivian fishing techniques with local fishermen during sunset and night fishing trips in extraordinary community settings."]},{"heading":"Enchanting Cultural Immersion","paragraphs":["Learn about local traditions, participate in community activities, and experience extraordinary Maldivian island life with captivating cultural exchanges."]},{"heading":"Sunset Cruises","paragraphs":["Enjoy breathtaking sunset cruises around the atoll, often combined with dolphin watching and traditional dhoni sailing in extraordinary waters."]},{"heading":"Community Life & Culture","paragraphs":["Fulidhoo is home to approximately 1,800 residents who maintain traditional Maldivian ways of life while embracing sustainable tourism. The island''s community is known for their exceptional friendliness, hospitality, and extraordinary cultural traditions that create a captivating atmosphere for visitors."]},{"heading":"Island Life","paragraphs":["Daily life on Fulidhoo follows traditional patterns centered around fishing, family, and community activities. The island maintains an extraordinary atmosphere where visitors can experience captivating Maldivian culture and customs in their most enchanting, remarkable setting."]},{"heading":"Local Traditions","paragraphs":["The community preserves traditional Maldivian practices including traditional music, dance, handicrafts, and fishing techniques. Visitors can observe and often participate in cultural activities and celebrations in this extraordinary island environment."]},{"heading":"Sustainable Tourism","paragraphs":["Fulidhoo has embraced sustainable tourism practices that benefit the local community while preserving the island''s natural environment and extraordinary cultural heritage for future generations to experience and enjoy."]}],"island_faqs":[{"question":"How do I get to Fulidhoo Island?","answer":"Regular ferry services are also available from Male and nearby islands in Vaavu Atoll."},{"question":"What is the best time to visit Fulidhoo?","answer":"The best time to visit Fulidhoo is during the dry season from December to April when weather conditions are most favorable for beach activities and water sports. However, the island can be visited year-round with the wet season offering fewer crowds and a more extraordinary local atmosphere."},{"question":"What accommodation options are available on Fulidhoo?","answer":"Fulidhoo offers various accommodations including extraordinary guesthouses and beachfront properties. Most accommodations offer air conditioning, private bathrooms, and meal packages in a captivating setting."},{"question":"What makes Fulidhoo''s charm special?","answer":"Fulidhoo is known for its extraordinary and captivating natural environment. The island maintains traditional Maldivian cultural practices while offering an enchanting atmosphere perfect for remarkable exploration. Visitors can experience exceptional cultural exchanges and participate in extraordinary community activities."}],"island_nearby_slugs":["keyodhoo","thinadhoo","rakeedhoo","felidhoo"]}'::jsonb
where node_type = 'location' and slug = 'fulidhoo';


